      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__micro-os-plus-diag-trace-c-api-main_1gaf651ff851996a49b25989c93118142f9" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int micro_os_plus_trace_putchar</definition>
        <argsstring>(int c)</argsstring>
        <name>micro_os_plus_trace_putchar</name>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
          <declname>c</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Write the single character to the trace output channel. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>c</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>A single byte character, passed as an <computeroutput>int</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The written character as an <computeroutput>int</computeroutput>, or EOF (-1) if an error occurred.</para>
</simplesect>
Converts <computeroutput>c</computeroutput> to <computeroutput>unsigned char</computeroutput> and passes it as a one-byte buffer to <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-diag-trace-c-api-implementation_1ga80d104ecf38dfcf40cae10bac0d2c562" kindref="member">micro_os_plus_trace_write</ref></computeroutput>. On success, returns the original value of <computeroutput>c</computeroutput>; on failure, returns EOF. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="/Users/ilg/MyProjects/micro-os-plus.github/xPacks/diag-trace-xpack.git/include/micro-os-plus/diag/trace/c-api.h" line="186" column="3" bodyfile="/Users/ilg/MyProjects/micro-os-plus.github/xPacks/diag-trace-xpack.git/src/trace-c-api.cpp" bodystart="97" bodyend="100" declfile="/Users/ilg/MyProjects/micro-os-plus.github/xPacks/diag-trace-xpack.git/include/micro-os-plus/diag/trace/c-api.h" declline="186" declcolumn="3"/>
        <references refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1trace_1_1detail_1_1tracer_1ad0af55a735d06c5c25c8bf38dc3fd4fd" compoundref="cpp-api-inlines_8h" startline="186" endline="198">micro_os_plus::trace::detail::tracer&lt; T &gt;::putchar</references>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__micro-os-plus-diag-trace-c-api-main_1ga378825eb60900b367774de9e76925b0d" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int micro_os_plus_trace_puts</definition>
        <argsstring>(const char *s)</argsstring>
        <name>micro_os_plus_trace_puts</name>
        <param>
          <type>const char *</type>
          <declname>s</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Write the string and a line terminator to the trace output channel. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>s</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>A null terminated string. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The total number of bytes written (string + newline), or EOF (-1) if an error occurred.</para>
</simplesect>
Writes the characters of <computeroutput>s</computeroutput> followed by a single newline character (<computeroutput>&apos;\n&apos;</computeroutput>). Unlike the standard C <computeroutput>puts()</computeroutput>, this function returns the total byte count written, not merely a non-negative indicator. If writing the newline fails after the string has been written successfully, EOF is returned. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
